            <ArticleTitle>Acute aortic dissection mimicking acute abdomen in a 14-year-old boy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1169-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/ped.12709</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aortic dissection is extremely rare in children. Although it usually presents with severe chest pain, atypical clinical presentations mimicking various illnesses may cause misdiagnosis. In this report, the case of a 14-year-old boy with symptoms suggestive of acute abdomen, which was finally diagnosed as aortic dissection, is discussed.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2015 Japan Pediatric Society.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
